cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "uniprotptmpy: A Python library for the UniProt PTM controlled vocabulary"
abstract: >-
  uniprotptmpy is a typed Python package for parsing and querying the UniProt
  post-translational modification (PTM) controlled vocabulary list. It parses
  the UniProt PTM list into structured PtmEntry objects covering feature
  types, taxonomic ranges, and cross-references, and exposes a queryable
  in-memory database with TSV export and a round-trip writer. An optional
  FastAPI and Model Context Protocol server exposes the same database over
  HTTP for interactive lookups and integration with proteomics tooling.
  uniprotptmpy is intended for proteomics software, annotation pipelines, and
  research scripts that need programmatic access to UniProt PTM terms. It
  requires Python 3.12 or later.
version: "0.2.1"
